 "details": {
  "title": "I’ll Be Seeing You",
  "lead": "The tune for trumpet, set on the bars of the Fret Finder guitar arrangement, which follows Michael Bublé’s record in his key, D♭ (E♭ for the trumpet), concert C4 to D♭5. It plays in that guitar track’s time, about 90. It follows Bublé where he leaves the book: the A he adds before the bridge, the held A over G♭ minor 6, rests where he barely sings, F then E♭ in the second verse again, and his longer last eight that holds the last D♭ over the G♭ chords. In the interlude, where he rests, the trumpet has a line of its own over the falling minor chords, ending on the G♭ minor sigh. The intro’s last bars and the ending share a short line: B♭, A♭, then A and G♭ over G♭ minor.",
  "facts": [
   [
    "Song",
    "Sammy Fain and Irving Kahal (1938)"
   ],
   [
    "Line",
    "The tune from the lead sheet, as Michael Bublé sings it on the Fret Finder page’s chords; the interlude line is new"
   ],
   [
    "Key",
    "D♭ major concert (E♭ for the trumpet), Bublé’s key"
   ],
   [
    "Form",
    "Intro, verse, bridge, verse, last eight, interlude, verse, longer last eight, ending"
   ],
   [
    "Plays with",
    "The guitar track on the Fret Finder page (ibsy-guitar.mp3), 3:18"
   ],
   [
    "Bars",
    "The ten intro bars come first, so bar 1 of the Fret Finder page is bar 11 here"
   ]
  ]
 }
